WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.047
Welcome to IAN 601, Introduction to Data Analytics Methods and Approaches.

00:00:07.047 --> 00:00:12.347
This course is designed to build your data analytics skills step by step,

00:00:12.347 --> 00:00:18.827
starting with Python fundamentals and gradually moving into practical data analysis.

00:00:18.827 --> 00:00:27.757
Across the fourteen modules, we begin with variables, decisions, functions, and core data structures.

00:00:27.757 --> 00:00:36.617
Then we move into organizing larger Python programs, more advanced Python techniques, professional coding practices,

00:00:36.617 --> 00:00:39.062
NumPy, and Pandas.

00:00:39.062 --> 00:00:46.482
In the later modules, we focus on advanced Pandas, data cleaning and exploratory analysis, statistics and visualization,

00:00:46.482 --> 00:00:54.426
and finally an introduction to machine learning and working with external data.

00:00:54.982 --> 00:00:58.154
Module 1 is where that foundation begins.

00:00:58.154 --> 00:01:07.459
We’ll learn how Python stores values, understands data types, performs calculations, and presents results clearly.

00:01:07.459 --> 00:01:10.494
You do not need to memorize every symbol.

00:01:10.494 --> 00:01:12.519
Focus on the logic.

00:01:12.519 --> 00:01:21.919
In analytics, we usually start with data, apply a rule or calculation, and produce a result that helps us answer a

00:01:21.919 --> 00:01:26.284
question. As we go, keep connecting the code to something real.

00:01:26.284 --> 00:01:31.659
A value might represent sales, cost, age, temperature, or another measurement.

00:01:31.659 --> 00:01:40.284
By the end of the module, you’ll combine these ideas in a small sales calculator and be able to explain what each line

00:01:40.284 --> 00:01:42.002
is doing.
